-the-sound-of-the-70s"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"MTV Beneficiaries (Low Budget Videos)","body":"This duo also benefited from MTV's launch, but their videos were \"fairly cheaply produced on videotape,\" focused on band performance, and were \"not especially cutting edge.\" \"And as I noted in our Darryl Hall and John Oats episode that duo also benefited from MTV's launch, but their videos were fairly cheaply produced on videotape, focused on band performance, and were not especially cutting edge.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"The British Are Charting Edition Part 2","url":null},{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"The British Are Charting Edition Part 2","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4f7a154465cd600c7ae7"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Philly Soul Roots Despite New York Move","body":"Even though Hall & Oates declined a contract with Philadelphia International Records and opted to relocate to New York for a different musical direction, their music consistently retained strong \"Philly Soul DNA\" and roots, demonstrating the lasting impact of their origins. \"But the roots are still there.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 37 - Philly Soul and the Sound of the 70s","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/ep-37-philly-soul-and-the-sound-of-the-70s"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Premiere Blue-Eyed Soul Act","body":"The duo of Daryl Hall and John Oates achieved significant success by topping both the pop and R&B charts with \"I Can't Go For That,\" becoming recognized as the premiere blue-eyed soul act of their day and demonstrating how artists can confound genre boundaries. \"I've chronicled how the duo of Darryl Hall and John Oates became the premiere blue-eyed soul act of their day, topping both the pop and R&B charts with I Can't Go For That.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit 